{#- drama_llama's cache-stable replacement for the Mistral Small 4
    (`mistral4`) stock template — see `templates/mistral4-gguf.jinja`
    for the detection key it replaces, and `src/baked.rs` for the
    loading ladder.

    The stock template cannot render an *open* assistant turn: it
    closes every assistant message with `</s>` unconditionally and has
    no `add_generation_prompt` branch at all, so the generation-prompt
    render is not a byte prefix of the follow-up render and every tool
    turn re-prefills. It also accepts reasoning only as a
    `thinking`-typed content chunk, never as a message field, so the
    dialect analyzer measures `ReasoningMode::None` and the `[THINK]`
    channel is invisible to the parser, the grammar and the re-render.

    What this template changes, and nothing else:

      1. `add_generation_prompt` is honoured by construction — the
         assistant close is emitted per *message*, and Mistral has no
         assistant header, so the generation prompt is simply the
         render up to that point.
      2. Reasoning round-trips as `[THINK]…[/THINK]`, one per thought,
         gated by `preserve_thinking` for aged turns (the
         Qwen-template convention `Session::from_engine` sets on every
         render).
      3. The turn renders in emission order from drama_llama's
         `chunks` (thoughts, prose and the calls where each sat)
         instead of merging prose into one slot and thoughts into
         one block — the model announces, then calls, and may think
         twice in a row. Without `chunks` (the dialect analyzer's
         probes), it renders from the `reasoning` / `reasoning_content`
         fields and `content_pre` / `content_post`.
      4. The 140-line Unsloth date-arithmetic preamble and the default
         Le Chat system message are GONE. That block injected today's
         and yesterday's date into the prompt *prefix*, so a session
         spanning midnight lost its entire cache. Persona and dates
         are app content under the 0.7 boundary; supply them in your
         own system prompt.
      5. The `raise_exception` role-alternation guard is dropped. Tool
         turns, mid-conversation system messages and consecutive user
         messages are all legal in a `Session` transcript.

    Framing (`<s>`, `</s>`, `[INST]`, `[SYSTEM_PROMPT]`,
    `[AVAILABLE_TOOLS]`, `[MODEL_SETTINGS]`, `[TOOL_CALLS]`, `[ARGS]`,
    `[TOOL_RESULTS]`, `[THINK]`) is byte-identical to stock — every one
    of those is a single special token in this model's vocab.
-#}
{{- '<s>' -}}

{#- System prompt. No default: the app owns persona content. -#}
{%- if messages and messages[0]['role'] == 'system' -%}
    {{- '[SYSTEM_PROMPT]' + messages[0]['content'] + '[/SYSTEM_PROMPT]' -}}
    {%- set loop_messages = messages[1:] -%}
{%- else -%}
    {%- set loop_messages = messages -%}
{%- endif -%}

{#- Tool definitions live in the static prefix, ahead of every
    message — the cache-friendly placement stock already chose. -#}
{%- if tools is defined and tools is not none and tools | length > 0 -%}
    {{- '[AVAILABLE_TOOLS]' + (tools | tojson) + '[/AVAILABLE_TOOLS]' -}}
{%- endif -%}

{#- Model settings. `reasoning_effort` is the trained switch for the
    `[THINK]` channel; drama_llama derives `enable_thinking` from
    `prompt.thinking`. NOTE this sits in the prompt PREFIX, so
    toggling thinking mid-conversation invalidates the whole cache —
    inherent to the format, same as Qwen's `enable_thinking`. -#}
{%- set reasoning_effort = 'high' if (enable_thinking is defined and enable_thinking) else 'none' -%}
{{- '[MODEL_SETTINGS]{"reasoning_effort": "' + reasoning_effort + '"}[/MODEL_SETTINGS]' -}}

{#- Pre-scan: index of the last user message, for the aged-reasoning
    guard below. -#}
{%- set ns_turn = namespace(last_user_idx=-1) -%}
{%- for i in range(loop_messages | length) -%}
    {%- if loop_messages[i]['role'] == 'user' -%}
        {%- set ns_turn.last_user_idx = i -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for message in loop_messages -%}
    {%- if message['role'] == 'user' -%}
        {{- '[INST]' + message['content'] + '[/INST]' -}}

    {%- elif message['role'] == 'system' -%}
        {#- Mid-conversation system turn. Stock raises; dropping it
            silently would be worse than rendering it in the format's
            own system framing. -#}
        {{- '[SYSTEM_PROMPT]' + message['content'] + '[/SYSTEM_PROMPT]' -}}

    {%- elif message['role'] == 'tool' -%}
        {{- '[TOOL_RESULTS]' + (message['content'] | string) + '[/TOOL_RESULTS]' -}}

    {%- elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
        {#- The turn renders from `chunks`, its blocks in emission order
            (drama_llama supplies them; stock Mistral reads the same
            text/thinking chunk list as `content`): each thought as its
            own `[THINK]…[/THINK]`, so back-to-back thoughts keep the
            markers between them, and prose where it sat. Without
            `chunks` the turn is rebuilt from the merged fields:
            reasoning, then the pre-call prose, the calls, the rest.
            `preserve_thinking` keeps a thought once a later user turn
            has aged it; without the flag an aged turn drops it and pays
            a one-turn re-prefill. Rendered VERBATIM — no `|trim`,
            byte-stability. -#}
        {%- set keep_thinking = (preserve_thinking is defined and preserve_thinking is true) or loop.index0 > ns_turn.last_user_idx -%}
        {%- set chunks = message.get('chunks') -%}
        {%- if chunks is none -%}
            {%- set thinking_text = message.get('reasoning') or message.get('reasoning_content') -%}
            {%- set chunks = [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': thinking_text}] if thinking_text else [] -%}
            {%- set has_split = message.get('content_pre') is not none -%}
            {%- set pre = message.get('content_pre') if has_split else message.get('content') -%}
            {%- if pre -%}
                {%- set chunks = chunks + [{'type': 'text', 'text': pre}] -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if message.get('tool_calls') -%}
                {%- set chunks = chunks + [{'type': 'tool_calls'}] -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if has_split and message.get('content_post') -%}
                {%- set chunks = chunks + [{'type': 'text', 'text': message['content_post']}] -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- for chunk in chunks -%}
            {%- if chunk['type'] == 'thinking' -%}
                {%- if keep_thinking -%}
                    {{- '[THINK]' + chunk['thinking'] + '[/THINK]' -}}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- elif chunk['type'] == 'text' -%}
                {{- chunk['text'] -}}
            {%- elif chunk['type'] == 'tool_calls' -%}
                {%- for tool_call in message['tool_calls'] -%}
                    {%- set function = tool_call['function'] -%}
                    {%- set arguments = function['arguments'] -%}
                    {#- `json_dumps`, not `tojson`: measured greedily with no
                        grammar, this model's unforced call spelling is
                        uniform `json.dumps` spacing (`": "` after keys,
                        `", "` between fields AND array elements) — see
                        `probe_unforced_habit::mistral4_unforced_call_spelling`.
                        Stock's `tojson` is compact, which would force the
                        model off its own habit to keep the round-trip
                        byte-stable (#85's lesson). The analyzer measures
                        this filter as `JsonSpacing::Spaced` and the grammar
                        prelude and `render_reference` follow it. -#}
                    {%- if arguments is not string -%}
                        {%- set arguments = arguments | json_dumps -%}
                    {%- elif arguments == '' -%}
                        {%- set arguments = '{}' -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{- '[TOOL_CALLS]' + function['name'] + '[ARGS]' + arguments -}}
                {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {#- Close the turn. Emitted per completed assistant message, so
            a generation prompt (no assistant message yet, or the open
            tail withheld by `render_with`) simply ends before it. -#}
        {{- '</s>' -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
